course: dictionary
lesson: 1967
title: Competitor in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A competitor is someone who is trying to win against others. In a race, a game or a contest, the competitors are all the people or teams taking part. In business, a competitor is a rival company that sells the same kind of thing. The words around the word show you which meaning is used.
explain: «Doping means athletes taking banned drugs to perform better; it cheats honest competitors and can badly harm health.» Here the competitors are the athletes in the contest. The clues are athletes, perform better and cheats: these people are all trying to win, and the cheating is unfair to the honest ones.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «It cheats honest people trying to win» still makes sense, so competitor fits. If you are not sure, look for clue words such as race, team, prize, shop or customers.
fact: A competitor is a person or team taking part in a race, contest or game, trying to win.
fact: A competitor can also be a business that sells the same kind of thing as another business and tries to get its customers.
fact: Competitors is the plural: more than one competitor.
fact: A fellow competitor is another person taking part alongside you.
fact: «Doping» means athletes taking banned drugs to perform better; it is cheating, and it is unfair to honest competitors.
exercise: «The competitors lined up at the start of the race.» Who are the competitors here? | The crowd cheering from the stands | *The runners and teams taking part in the race | The coach who drove the bus | The judges who count the points
exercise: Mia's bakery and the shop across the road both sell the same bread. In business, what is the shop across the road to Mia's bakery? | A ticket | A teacher | A sports team | *A competitor
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Doping means athletes taking banned drugs to perform better; it cheats honest competitors and can badly harm health.» that means people trying to win against others. | health | *competitors | honest | cheats
test: «Ten competitors finished the race, and three of them were from our school.» How many competitors finished the race? | Thirty | Three | Seven | *Ten
test: What does «fellow competitor» mean? | *Another person taking part with you | A prize for the winner | A judge who gives out points | A person who runs a shop
exam: In «Doping... cheats honest competitors», who are the competitors? | Coaches who train the athletes | Drugs that make athletes ill | *Athletes and teams trying to win the race fairly | Judges who score the race
